course: dictionary
lesson: 10192
title: Timid: shy and not brave
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence around it tells you which one. «Timid» can mean shy and easily frightened, like a timid animal. It can also mean not daring or strong, like a timid attempt.
explain: Look for clues. In «a timid, bedraggled weasel, one of last night's prisoners», the weasel is worn out and nervous, so timid describes how it feels. In «timid scavengers that shoal for safety», the fish stick together to stay safe, which shows they are shy rather than fierce.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. Does "shy and easily frightened" fit? If it does, you have the right meaning. Brave and bold are the opposites of timid.
fact: Timid means shy and nervous, easily frightened, and not brave or confident.
fact: «Timid» can also describe a weak effort, such as a timid attempt, which is a try that is not bold or strong.
fact: Timid is an adjective. Its comparisons are timider or more timid, and timidest or most timid.
fact: Useful phrases are «a timid smile», «timid animal» and «shy and timid».
fact: Real piranhas are mostly timid shoaling fish and scavengers, so the fierce picture in cartoons is not the whole truth.
exercise: In «a timid, bedraggled weasel, one of last night's prisoners», what does timid mean? | Brightly coloured | Loud and cheeky | Very fast | *Shy and nervous
exercise: «Piranhas have razor-sharp teeth... but most are timid scavengers that shoal for safety.» Why do these fish shoal? | *To stay safe together in a group | To hunt bigger animals alone | To make a loud noise | To show off to the other fish
exercise: Which of these describes a timid smile? | A smile that shows all the teeth | A smile made while shouting | *A small, shy smile | A big, laughing grin
test: «Cartoons show piranhas stripping a cow to bones in seconds; real piranhas are mostly timid shoaling fish.» What are real piranhas mostly like? | Very tall and bold | Slow and sleepy | Always fierce and loud | *Timid, shy and shoaling, not always fierce
test: What does «a timid attempt» suggest? | *A try that is weak and not bold | A huge, bold try that wins | A try that was finished very quickly | A try made in a loud voice
exam: Which word is closest in meaning to timid? | Bold | *Shy | Loud | Quick
